Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Working as a researcher at Cambridge Section - Jobs Browse our vacancies Academic vacancies Professional services vacancies Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? How to apply Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs What's the research culture like at the University of Cambridge? At the University of Cambridge, we’re at the forefront of global research. Renowned for our pioneering contributions across disciplines, we aim to foster a vibrant research environment that blends tradition with innovation. Researchers here are empowered by a culture of intellectual freedom, interdisciplinary collaboration, and access to world-class facilities. Scholars here are free to pursue transformative ideas and tackle some of the most pressing challenges of our time. Our researchers are driving breakthroughs in cancer care, highlighting the university’s powerful blend of clinical expertise and cutting-edge science. They’re leading bold, interdisciplinary projects in the fields of technology and sustainability – from engineering programmable plants to advancing robotics through major national initiatives. It’s a place where world-changing ideas are not only imagined – they’re realised. At Cambridge, you can become part of a dynamic, supportive community that values curiosity, creativity, and collaboration. We’re right at the centre of UK innovation, connecting academia, industry, and policy. It’s an inspiring environment where researchers at every stage can thrive and make a lasting difference. As a researcher at Cambridge, you can: Participate in our new annual Academic Career Pathways (Research) promotions scheme, offering progression to more senior research roles. Apply for pay progression within your current band, through our termly Researcher Contribution Increment scheme. Get support from the University’s Postdoc Academy, who enable our Postdocs to realise their potential through information, community, advocacy and professional development. View current researcher vacancies Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
