    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/director-cancer-research-uk-cambridge-institute-sw50928": {
      "title": "Director, Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute",
      "description": "Director, Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Director, Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Director, Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute The Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute is one of the world's leading centres for cancer discovery research. The Institute is one of Cancer Research UK's (CRUK) core-funded Institutes, the largest constituent of the CRUK Cambridge Centre and a department of the University of Cambridge. It is home to approximately 450 staff and students and receives around £25 million in annual core funding from CRUK. The University of Cambridge, in partnership with CRUK, seeks a new Director of the Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute. The successful candidate will also serve as a Senior Group Leader, maintaining an internationally leading research programme supported by world-class facilities, scientific infrastructure and long-term investment. The Institute is dedicated to improving patient lives through discovery science. Its research seeks to transform understanding of every stage of the tumour lifecycle, generating the biological insights that underpin future advances in cancer prevention, diagnosis and treatment. Located on the Cambridge Biomedical Campus, it benefits from close connections with Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust, the CRUK Cambridge Centre, AstraZeneca, alongside a range of other academic, healthcare and industry partners. Together, these relationships create a uniquely potent environment in which to accelerate the translation of discovery science into patient benefit. Researchers also benefit from access to eleven state-of-the-art core facilities, substantial long-term investment and a funding model designed to support ambitious, high-impact science. The new Director will provide inspirational scientific leadership to the Institute and will be responsible for its ongoing strategic development, ensuring that its research programmes remain at the forefront of cancer science globally. Working closely with CRUK, the University of Cambridge and the Institute Executive Committee, the Director will shape the scientific direction of the Institute, guide major research investments and oversee the development of new scientific capabilities. They will ensure the Institute continues to maximise opportunities presented by emerging technologies, including advances in data science and artificial intelligence. Furthermore, the Director will have a large degree of autonomy in establishing the scientific direction and priorities of the Institute, presenting a unique opportunity for an exceptional leader to shape and drive one of the world's foremost cancer research organisations. As one of the most senior and visible scientific leaders within CRUK, they will contribute to the development of national and international cancer research strategy, act as an ambassador for the Institute and CRUK, and help ensure that the Institute continues to make a leading contribution to cancer research globally. The successful candidate will be an exceptional researcher in their own right and will have an outstanding international scientific reputation in cancer research or a closely related field. They will possess a vision for the institute, and leadership required to enact this vision, building upon the Institute's achievements to date and directing its next phase of development. The Director will embody the ambition and values of both the Institute and CRUK and will lead one of the world's premier cancer research institutes into the future. Enquiries can be made, in confidence, to Natalie Derry or Jamie Cumming-Wesley at WittKieffer. Completed applications should be submitted electronically to rsmith@wittkieffer.com Applications should consist of a CV accompanied by a covering letter addressing the criteria in the person specification and motivation for applying. The deadline for receipt of applications is noon on 19 October 2026 The final interviews will take place January 2027. For further information, please visit: https://wittkieffer.com/positions/a1wun0000022oohmau Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference SW50928 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cancer Research UK Cambridge Institute Salary Reference SW50928 Category Professorships and Directorships Date published 2 September 2026 Closing date 19 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-associate-in-islamic-art-fixed-term-vn50843": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Islamic Art (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Associate in Islamic Art (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Associate in Islamic Art (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Associate in Islamic Art (Fixed Term) The HRH Prince Alwaleed Bin Talal Centre of Islamic Studies (CIS) at the University of Cambridge is seeking to appoint a Postdoctoral Research and Outreach Associate in Islamic art and architecture and/or material culture. The post is a three-year, fixed-term position which will commence in September 2027. It is full-time and based in the Centre of Islamic Studies, which is located in the Faculty of Asian and Middle Eastern Studies. CIS research and outreach posts are distinctive in that postholders are expected to 1) pursue a research project in an area of Islamic art, architecture and/or material culture and 2) design and run a set of outreach activities that reach beyond the academic community. What form the latter will take will depend on the specialism of the appointee but collaboration with the Fitzwilliam Museum, other Cambridge museums, the University Library and local schools is welcomed, as well as proposals for other forms of outreach. A current project with a strong outreach component is Dr Zahra Kazani's Botanical Wisdom: Art, Medicine, and Nature in Muslim Societies ( https://www.cis.cam.ac.uk/research/post/botanical-wisdom-art-medicine-and-nature-in-muslim-societies/ ). CIS is one of a network of HRH Alwaleed Bin Talal centres and research and outreach associates are strongly encouraged to collaborate with colleagues at our UK partner institution, the Alwaleed Centre at the University of Edinburgh and with other Alwaleed centres at Harvard, Georgetown, the American University of Beirut and the American University of Cairo as appropriate. Research and outreach associates are expected to apply for additional external funding for the activities they design, when possible. The postholder may also contribute to the teaching of Islamic art, architecture and material culture within the Department of Middle Eastern Studies, with which CIS has close links, or elsewhere in the University. Candidates will need to demonstrate an upward research trajectory and an ability to develop and carry out research projects of a high academic standard. They will also need to show an interest in and understanding of the remit of the Centre of Islamic Studies and a commitment to outreach beyond academia. Attendance at and participation in CIS weekly seminars and events during term-time, and annual conferences or symposia, is expected. The role requires an ability to work independently but also as part of a team, and native or near native fluency in spoken and written English. The successful candidate will be expected to have been awarded their PhD by the date their employment commences. CIS Research and Outreach posts are intended primarily for early-career researchers. Applications are therefore invited from researchers who have submitted their doctoral thesis for viva voce examination no more than four years prior to the application closing date. Those wishing to make a case for a career break due to maternity leave, family commitments, illness, or other exceptional circumstances should provide relevant details. Please note that time spent working outside academia does not qualify as a career break. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for applications is 15 October 2026. Academic references will be requested for shortlisted candidates in advance of the interviews, which will likely take place towards the end of November. They may take place in-person or online, depending on the applicant's and interviewers' availability. Any offer of employment will be conditional on the offer-holder having or gaining the right to work in the UK and receipt of a satisfactory workplace reference if relevant. Further enquiries may be directed to enquiries@cis.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference VN50843 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location HRH Prince Alwaleed Bin Talal Centre of Islamic Studies Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference VN50843 Category Research Date published 24 August 2026 Closing date 15 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/administrative-assistant-part-time-fixed-term-rc50911": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Administrative Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Administrative Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) We are looking to recruit an enthusiastic and motivated Administrative Assistant to support Professor Virginia Newcombe's research group, working across two multi-centre studies focused improving how we diagnose and predict outcome after mild traumatic brain injury. The role will be based in Cambridge, within the Perioperative, Acute, Critical Care and Emergency Medicine (PACE) Section, Department of Medicine. The appointee will provide essential administrative support to ensure the smooth running of these clinical studies, including financial administration, processing participant expense payments, preparing questionnaire packs, data entry and verification, and providing support for project meetings. The role also includes acting as personal assistant to Professor Newcombe and providing cross-cover support with the PACE Section's departmental administrator. The post holder will receive appropriate training as required. The appointee will have relevant administrative experience, ideally within a research, university, or NHS setting. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to handle confidential information appropriately are essential. Experience of financial administration or working within a clinical research environment would be advantageous. The position will be based in the Cambridge Biomedical Campus. Applicants will be expected to work collaboratively with colleagues and contribute to a positive and dynamic research environment. Informal enquiries are welcome and can be directed to Professor Virginia Newcombe ( vfjn2@cam.ac.uk ). Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 December 2028 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RC50911 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Medicine Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference RC50911 Category Assistant staff Date published 28 August 2026 Closing date 17 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/admissions-administrator-temporary-cover-ea50469": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Admissions Administrator [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Admissions Administrator [Temporary Cover] Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Admissions Administrator [Temporary Cover] Location Madingley Hall is part of the Institute of Continuing Education in the University of Cambridge, Built in the 16th century, this elegant country house has 16 well-equipped meeting rooms, 62 ensuite bedrooms, a professional kitchen, licensed bar, coffee shop, Lodge House available as rentable short-stay accommodation and is set in 8-acres of grounds including superb Capability Brown designed gardens. The Role The ideal candidate will be well-organised with excellent communication skills. You will have the ability to work accurately and efficiently without close supervision and have good interpersonal skills to be able to deal effectively with a wide range of people. You will ideally have experience of admissions or customer enquiries in a Higher Education environment, and previous experience of working with CamSIS or Salesforce would be beneficial. The role-holders will assist in the administration of student enquiries and admissions, for all PACE Undergraduate and Postgraduate courses at PACE and for MSt courses across the University. They play an important role as the 'public face' of PACE providing an efficient and informative enrolments and admissions service to prospective, new and returning students. Student applications are received via the University's student records systems and training will be provided where necessary. Benefits 36 days annual leave, inclusive of Bank Holidays Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Support for health & mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Rental deposit scheme Public transport season ticket loans Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term for 18 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Further information is available at the link below. Informal enquiries are encouraged and can be made to Antony Bounds antony.bounds@pace.cam.ac.uk Questions about the application process may be directed to: HR@pace.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is 4th October 2026\nInterviews will take place on 26th October 2026 Please quote reference EA50469 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Admission Administrator Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Institute of Professional and Continuing Education Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference EA50469 Category Assistant staff Date published 1 September 2026 Closing date 4 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
