    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/chef-manager-xm50832": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Chef Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Chef Manager Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Chef Manager We are seeking an enthusiastic and experienced Café Chef Manager to lead the daily operations of Scholars Brew, our busy and vibrant café. This is an exciting opportunity for a hospitality professional with a passion for fresh food, exceptional customer service, and team leadership within a dynamic academic environment. The successful candidate will be responsible for overseeing all aspects of the café's operation, including menu planning, food preparation, stock control, financial performance, and the management and development of the café team. You will play a key role in ensuring a welcoming atmosphere, delivering consistently high-quality food and beverages, and maintaining excellent standards of food safety, hygiene, and customer care. We are looking for an individual who combines strong culinary skills with effective leadership and organisational abilities. The ideal candidate will be proactive, customer-focused, and committed to driving innovation and continuous improvement while building a positive and supportive team culture. This role offers the opportunity to make a significant contribution to the ongoing success of Scholars Brew while developing your career within a professional and supportive catering and hospitality team. Benefits of working at the University of Cambridge include: Competitive pay with automatic annual cost of living increases and service-related progression. Generous annual leave entitlement, helping you maintain a healthy work-life balance. Flexible and hybrid working arrangements to support your lifestyle and wellbeing. Family-friendly policies, including enhanced maternity, adoption, and shared parental leave, plus access to workplace nurseries. Excellent pension scheme with a generous employer contribution through auto-enrolment. Travel and shopping discounts at over 2,000 local and national retailers. Relocation support for eligible new starters. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early if we receive sufficient applications for the role. Therefore, if you are interested, please submit your application as early as possible. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference XM50832 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Chef Manager Key information Department/location Estates Division (Business Services) Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference XM50832 Category Assistant staff Date published 25 August 2026 Closing date 9 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/citiid-phd-programme-in-immunity-and-infection-phd-studentship-fixed-term-rc50887": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "CITIID PhD Programme in Immunity and Infection PhD Studentship (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs CITIID PhD Programme in Immunity and Infection PhD Studentship (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs CITIID PhD Programme in Immunity and Infection PhD Studentship (Fixed Term) We are pleased to announce a PhD position, centred at the \"Cambridge Institute of Therapeutic Immunology and Infectious Disease (CITIID)\", within the Department of Medicine at the University of Cambridge School of Clinical Medicine. CITIID aims to support both fundamental and translational research in immunity, infection, and inflammation https://www.citiid.cam.ac.uk/ The objectives of this post are to provide a rigorous training, cutting-edge skills and broad academic insight and expertise to bring novel approaches to the study of immune, infectious, and inflammatory disorders. The student will be offered a range of study options, with the objectives of improving our knowledge and understanding of the pathogenesis of infectious, immune and inflammatory disorders. Students are encouraged to broaden their interests and are not expected to apply with a specific supervisor/laboratory in mind. The first few weeks of training involves the opportunity to work with in different group leaders prior to choosing which laboratory they would like to pursue their 3.5-year PhD thesis project. In addition to 'state of the art' research facilities, students will have access to a wide variety of training and researcher development activities, many of which are offered through the Graduate School of Life Sciences and the wider University. Eligibility Academic requirements: At least a 2:1 Honours degree from a UK university or equivalent in a related topic. If your degree is not from the UK, please check International Qualifications to find the equivalent in your country. English language requirements: The University requires a high level of proficiency in English. For details, click here: http://www.graduate.study.cam.ac.uk/international-students/competence-english/will-i-have-language-requirement Residence Eligibility: UK students will be eligible for a full studentship, covering the costs of Home fees and a stipend (currently) of £18,500 per annum for 4 years. Further information on how your fee status is determined can be found here: https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/finance/fees/what-my-fee-status Apply via the University online application portal: https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/courses/directory/cvmdpdmed Click here for full details and instructions http://www.graduate.study.cam.ac.uk/how-do-i-apply Please include in your CV a short summary of any previous research experience you may have had. For general enquiries, please email the Postgraduate Administrator:\nEmail: pgmed@medschl.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is 1 October 2026 Interviews: 19 October 2026 Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 4 years in the first instance. Please quote reference RC50887 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Key information Department/location Department of Medicine Salary Reference RC50887 Category Studentships Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 1 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/collections-and-participation-digital-fixed-term-pe50867": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Collections and Participation (Digital) (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Collections and Participation (Digital) (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Collections and Participation (Digital) (Fixed Term) We are looking for a Research Associate to lead on digital participation within Collections-Connections-Communities (CCC), a Strategic Research Initiative at the University of Cambridge which empowers researchers to use the University's collections  the UK's highest concentration of internationally important collections outside London  to address the big questions of our time. This is a fixed-term post within a new Collections and Participation team, funded for one year in the first instance with potential to extend to July 2030, dedicated to bringing communities especially those that are underrepresented or underserved into research and practice within the University's collections. You will work alongside a Programmes Coordinator, a Research Associate focused on in-person participation, and a Natural History Engagement Coordinator. You will co-design and deliver scalable, ethical, innovative and replicable projects with digital participation at their core, using methods that may include crowdsourcing, citizen science and the responsible use of AI tools for GLAM collections. You will develop and support online communities of co-researchers, nurture partnerships with digital, curatorial, learning and conservation colleagues, and translate advances in the field into scalable frameworks for digital participatory research. You will disseminate your work through publications and conference presentations, build capacity for reflective practice across the collections, prepare funding proposals, monitor budgets, line-manage freelancers, and work with a new Impact & Evaluation team in University of Cambridge Museums to refine digital participation activity. We're looking for someone with experience of co-designing, managing, delivering and evaluating collections-based participation programmes in a digital environment, and research experience with sufficient breadth and depth of specialist knowledge of digital participation methodologies, evidenced by peer-reviewed research which may be co-authored or by conference papers. Strong digital skills, including the use of AI tools for GLAM collections and an awareness of the issues surrounding their responsible use, are essential, as are experience of working across multiple collections and stakeholders, of line-managing freelancers, knowledge of ethical frameworks and data protection principles, and a postgraduate degree or equivalent collections experience. An understanding of Knowledge Exchange and Impact Pathways would be an advantage. Digital environments offer extraordinary potential for community participation with Cambridge's collections, and this role exists to realise it across an entire collections ecosystem rather than a single institution. You will have an activity budget, a group of experienced mentors, and real scope to define what responsible digital participation looks like for the sector. Occasional evening and weekend working will be required. If you'd like to open up centuries of collections to people who have never been able to reach them, we'd love to hear from you. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 1 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For any questions relating to this recruitment please contact admin@botanic.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Role Profile/Further information Key information Department/location Botanic Garden Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference PE50867 Category Academic-related Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 11 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/collections-and-participation-fixed-term-pe50866": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) We are looking for a Research Associate to join Collections-Connections-Communities (CCC), a Strategic Research Initiative at the University of Cambridge which empowers researchers to use the University's collections ¿ the UK's highest concentration of internationally important collections outside London to address the big questions of our time. This is a fixed-term post within a new Collections & Participation team, funded for one year in the first instance with potential for future funding to July 2030, dedicated to bringing communities especially those that are underrepresented or underserved into research and practice within the University's collections. You will work alongside a Programmes Coordinator, a Research Associate focused on digital participation, and a Natural History Engagement Coordinator. You will co-design and deliver scalable, ethical, innovative and replicable projects using participatory methodologies, working with new and existing community partners through an agreed framework of ethics and care. You will nurture partnerships with curatorial, conservation, learning and public programmes colleagues, disseminate your work through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and build capacity across the University's collections by offering training in participation methods. You will engage with evidence on community needs across the city and region, prepare funding proposals, monitor budgets, line-manage freelancers, and work with a new Impact & Evaluation team in University of Cambridge Museums to test and refine participation activity. We're looking for someone with experience of co-designing, managing, delivering and evaluating collections-based participation programmes, and research experience with sufficient breadth and depth of specialist knowledge of participatory methodologies, evidenced by peer-reviewed research ¿ which may be co-authored or by conference papers. Experience of working across multiple collections and stakeholders while navigating conflicting priorities, of line-managing freelancers, and knowledge of ethical frameworks and data protection principles are essential, as is a postgraduate degree or equivalent collections experience of working with communities. A strong commitment to social justice and inclusive practice, and an understanding of Knowledge Exchange and Impact Pathways, would serve you well. This is a rare chance to develop participatory research practice across an entire collections ecosystem rather than a single institution, with an activity budget of your own, a group of mentors with deep experience of participation in collections, and real scope to change practice in the sector. Occasional evening and weekend working will be required alongside the delivery of participation activities. If you'd like to help transform the relationship between Cambridge's collections and the communities around them, we'd love to hear from you. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 1 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For any questions relating to this recruitment please contact admin@botanic.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Role Profile/Further information Key information Department/location Botanic Garden Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference PE50866 Category Academic-related Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 11 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
