ngs Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Coordinator [Undergraduate] [Full-time, Maternity Cover] Applications are invited for an organised and experienced administrator for the Department of Politics and International Studies (POLIS). This role with a special emphasis on undergraduate programmes. The post holder will be the principal administrator for all POLIS tracks within the HSPS Tripos as well as shared papers on the History and Politics Tripos.  The role has oversight of all administrative elements until final examination and has line management responsibilities. Maternity cover: This post is fixed-term for 12 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for applications is: Wednesday 09 September 2026. The interview date is expected to be: Week  commencing 21 September 2026 Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to:Business Operations Manager Helen Reynolds BOM@polis.cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: hr@hsps.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference UE50803 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Politics and International Studies Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference UE50803 Category Assistant staff Date published 20 August 2026 Closing date 9 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
