    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/copywriter-and-content-editor-ea50845": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Copywriter and Content Editor | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Copywriter and Content Editor Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Copywriter and Content Editor Are you a writer and content editor passionate about bringing campaigns and stories to life for diverse audiences across multiple channels? Do you thrive in managing website content, and translating complex information into accessible messaging? Join us to create and shape content for a world-renowned educational institution as part of a new content team. At University of Cambridge Professional and Continuing Education (PACE), our mission is to make lifelong learning accessible to all. We design and deliver a diverse portfolio of world-class short courses and qualifications. Continuing education is one of the most dynamic and fast-evolving areas in both UK and global higher education. As a recognised leader in the field, tracing our roots back to 1873, we offer high-quality programmes for adult learners, many of whom study part-time for personal enrichment or professional growth. We're passionate about what we do, and your ideas and contributions will be valued. The Role Reporting to the Content Manager and working alongside the Visual Content Creator, you'll be part of a collaborative marketing and external engagement team. You'll write content across our website, campaigns, and wider communications, ensuring it engages with our audiences and supports organisational priorities. You'll champion our verbal identity. And you'll combine creativity with efficiency using AI-enabled tools. Some of what you'll do: Write, review and edit copy to create engaging, on-brand and search-optimised content, from course pages to campaign copy, across our channels. Develop content aligned to briefs and campaign objectives. Lead in the adoption, use and governance of AI-supported content tools. Manage website content, ensuring clarity, accuracy, accessibility, and consistency. Develop and carry out search optimisation planning and implementation. You'll have: Experience in content editing and copywriting roles producing high-quality written content across formats and channels for different audiences. Excellent ideation, development and problem-solving skills, able to translate briefs into compelling, actionable concepts and resolve content creation and content management challenges. Experience in website content management, including CMS systems (ideally Drupal), and analytics tools. Excellent editing and proofreading skills. Excellent understanding of brand identity and experience in applying guidelines. The ability to collaborate with colleagues, stakeholders and external production partners. Strong organisational and planning skills. Strong understanding of and experience in SEO and GEO. A degree or equivalent professional experience. What we offer: The starting salary would typically be the entry-point of the band advertised, increasing annually. Benefits 36 days annual leave, inclusive of Bank Holidays Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Family-friendly initiatives Career and professional development opportunities Support for health & mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Rental deposit scheme Public transport season ticket loans Working arrangements We welcome applications from individuals interested in flexible working arrangements within our core team hours of 8am to 5.30pm, Monday to Friday. Elements of this role are suitable for hybrid working, where staff can split their time between in-person collaboration and remote working. The frequency of the remote elements of the role can be discussed with the recruiting manager. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. As part of your application, please include links to 5 published writing samples (with no more than 2 longform examples, max 2000 words each). We'll review these as part of our selection process, in line with the person specification in the 'Further information' document. The closing date for applications is 18 September. Interviews will take place on 01 October (online), followed by a second round of interviews (plus task) for shortlisted applicants on 07 October (in person). Informal enquiries can be made to the Content Manager andrea.hunt@pace.cam.ac.uk Enquires about the application process should be directed to HR@pace.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference EA50845 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Copywriter and Content Editor Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Institute of Professional and Continuing Education Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference EA50845 Category Assistant staff Date published 25 August 2026 Closing date 18 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
