    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/electronics-design-engineer-ka49997": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Electronics Design Engineer | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Electronics Design Engineer Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Electronics Design Engineer The Cavendish Laboratory is the place of pioneering physics, that's been at the forefront of scientific discovery for 150 years, and will continue to be, because we never sit still. The Cavendish Laboratory has made several important discoveries, including: the discovery of the electron (1897), the neutron (1932), the structure of DNA (1953); thirty Cavendish researchers have won Nobel Prizes. We're trailblazers who continue to extend the frontiers of physics. The Department has moved into our new state-of-the-art, multi-million pound Ray Dolby Centre which will be the centrepiece of the new Cavendish Laboratory. This is an exciting and challenging time for the Department, and we would like to find a highly motivated individual with a positive attitude towards change and development to join us. A reorganisation and merger of several professional services teams within the Department of Physics has led to the creation of Cavendish Engineering - one of the largest, most advanced multidisciplinary university workshops within the UK. We are looking for someone with a very strong electronics background, who wants to be challenged with unique problems daily - regularly back to first principles, with no two days likely to be the same.    If this sounds like you, we'd love to hear from you. We encourage early applications as they will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. Previous applicants need not apply. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcome and should be sent to Ceri Williamson, Head of Cavendish Engineering ( caw204@cam.ac.uk ) Please quote reference KA49997 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Physics Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference KA49997 Category Assistant staff Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 23 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/finance-coordinator-jk50430": {
      "title": "Finance Coordinator",
      "description": "Finance Coordinator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Finance Coordinator Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Finance Coordinator The Faculty of Law is one of the world's leading institutions for legal research and teaching. We are seeking a proactive and experienced Finance Coordinator to play a key role in supporting the Faculty's financial management and ensuring that financial resources are used effectively to support the Faculty's objectives, academic activities, and strategies. Working closely with a variety of colleagues across the Faculty, you will provide financial advice and management information to support planning and decision-making. You will oversee a wide range of financial activities, including budgeting, forecasting, financial reporting, research grant administration, and compliance with University financial regulations. This is an excellent opportunity for a finance professional who enjoys working collaboratively, analysing complex financial information, and improving processes in a busy, changing, and intellectually stimulating environment. The role offers significant responsibility and variety, with opportunities to contribute to strategic planning, support major academic initiatives, and work with colleagues across the wider University finance community. At present, the University is undergoing an institutional change in its financial processes, practices, and systems. As such, a successful applicant would be expected to play a large role in facilitating the changes, including liaising with central Finance Division colleagues, communicating important information to Faculty staff, and quickly learning new systems. Key responsibilities With the Deputy Faculty Manager (Finance, Research & Facilities Management), produce and analyse management accounts, budgets, forecasts, and financial reports to support effective financial planning and decision-making across the Faculty. Provide financial advice and guidance to a variety of stakeholders within the Faculty, budget holders and colleagues on financial planning, policies and procedures. Monitor income and expenditure, identify financial risks and opportunities, and support the development of financial plans and cost-saving initiatives. With the Research Grants Administrator and relevant academic colleagues, manage and monitor research grant expenditure, providing advice on funding, budgeting and compliance requirements. Ensure Faculty financial procedures comply with University regulations and contribute to the review and improvement of local processes and controls. Maintain the integrity of financial data, undertake reconciliations, investigate discrepancies and support financial reporting requirements. Act as a key liaison with the School of the Humanities & Social Sciences Finance Team, the University's Finance Division and contribute to University-wide finance initiatives and networks. Support and oversee day-to-day finance operations in the Faculty, including purchasing, invoicing, and other financial system processes. Line manage the Faculty's Finance Administrator role, working closely with the position to carry out all functions of the Finance office. About you You will have substantial experience in a finance role, excellent analytical and organisational skills, and the ability to communicate financial information clearly to both financial and non-financial audiences. You will be comfortable working independently, managing competing priorities, and building effective working relationships across a diverse academic community. Experience of financial management within a higher education or similarly complex organisation would be advantageous. The closing date for the role is 23 September 2026. Interviews will take place on 7th October 2026 at the Faculty of Law. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference JK50430 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Faculty of Law Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference JK50430 Category Assistant staff Date published 11 August 2026 Closing date 23 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
