    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/fundraising-assistant-dh50787": {
      "title": "Fundraising Assistant",
      "description": "Fundraising Assistant | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Fundraising Assistant Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Fundraising Assistant Are you an organised and proactive administrator looking to build a career in fundraising and higher education? This is your chance to support world-class fundraising at one of the globe's leading universities, helping to drive research, teaching, and innovation that changes lives. As a Fundraising Assistant , you'll provide high-level administrative and operational support to our fundraising team. Working closely with senior fundraisers, academics, and external partners, you'll help manage donor relationships, support international travel and events, maintain accurate fundraising records, and contribute to projects that directly impact the University's future. What you'll do: Coordinate complex diaries, meetings, travel, and high-profile events. Act as the first point of contact for senior donors, volunteers, and University leaders. Support fundraising operations through data management, reporting, and process improvements. Assist with prospect research and briefing materials to support senior fundraisers. Provide administrative and financial process support across the team. What we're looking for: Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritise competing deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Confidence using Microsoft Office and databases (experience with fundraising databases is desirable). A professional, discreet approach to handling sensitive information. A collaborative team player with initiative and problem-solving ability. Why join us? This is a fantastic opportunity to grow your skills in a dynamic fundraising environment. At Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations, we support research, education and innovation tackling global challenges, from climate change to public health. Meaningful work Your role contributes to initiatives that make a real difference. Inclusive culture We value different perspectives and aim to create a place where everyone feels they belong. Development and growth Access training, mentoring and the wider Cambridge network to build your career. Wellbeing and flexibility We offer flexible working, generous leave and wellbeing support. Strong team and resources You'll work with experienced colleagues, good systems and a supportive environment. Our commitment to inclusion We welcome applications from all backgrounds and communities. If you need adjustments at any stage, we'll support you. Interested? If you're looking for a role where your work matters and you can grow, we'd like to hear from you. University of Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations - do your best work here. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure you read the candidate pack attached and that you detail your career history and outline your suitability for the role in your application. The closing date for this position is midnight on Sunday the 13th of September 2026. Interviews for this position are anticipated to take place on week commencing the 21st of September 2026. Please quote reference DH50787 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Candidate Pack - Fundraising Assistant - August 2026 Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference DH50787 Category Assistant staff Date published 21 August 2026 Closing date 13 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/global-trips-associate-secondment-dh50644": {
      "title": "Global Trips Associate (Secondment)",
      "description": "Global Trips Associate (Secondment) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Global Trips Associate (Secondment) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Global Trips Associate (Secondment) We are delighted to be offering a one-year secondment opportunity for current University of Cambridge staff to join Development and Alumni Relations as our Global Trips Associate . You'll help coordinate a complex programme of high-profile international visits supporting Cambridge's global engagement and fundraising ambitions as we prepare to launch our next major fundraising campaign. These visits will involve University leaders, key supporters, alumni, donors and partners around the world, giving you the opportunity to work across a wide range of teams and engage with senior stakeholders across the University. Why this role? Why now? This is an exciting time to join Cambridge as we prepare to launch one of the most ambitious fundraising campaigns in the University's history. University leaders will be travelling extensively to key international markets to build momentum, strengthen relationships and deliver campaign launch activity. As Global Trips Associate, you'll be at the heart of making these visits happen. You'll bring together multiple teams, stakeholders and objectives, making sure programmes are carefully planned, everyone is well briefed and opportunities are maximised. What you'll do: Coordinate complex international visits from initial planning through to delivery and follow-up. Bring together itineraries, briefings, country specific information, visas and other supporting materials. Work closely with colleagues across development, alumni engagement, events and the wider University to ensure activity is joined up and delivered effectively. Coordinate internal and external stakeholders, tracking actions and ensuring plans and deadlines stay on track. Provide advice and guidance on international travel, logistics, risk and operational requirements. Who we're looking for: We're looking for an organised, proactive and confident colleague with experience coordinating complex international travel, logistics, programmes or similar projects. You'll be comfortable managing competing priorities and have the judgement and problem-solving skills to anticipate challenges and find solutions. You'll have: Significant experience coordinating complex travel, logistics or similar projects involving multiple people. Experience supporting senior stakeholders with travel or programme activity. Excellent organisational and planning skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and complex schedules. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, including confidence working with senior colleagues and external partners. Excellent attention to detail and the ability to produce accurate, high-quality documentation. Experience developing or improving processes, systems or guidance. The ability to work independently and exercise sound judgement. Why join Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations? Working in Development and Alumni Relations means joining a mission-driven community helping unlock the potential of one of the world's most influential universities. A meaningful mission Your work will support Cambridge's global engagement and fundraising ambitions, helping strengthen relationships with alumni, supporters and partners around the world. A collaborative environment You'll work alongside colleagues across the department and the wider University, gaining insight into the international activity supporting a major fundraising campaign. Wellbeing and balance Flexible working, generous leave and wellbeing resources help you thrive professionally and personally. Diversity and belonging We value different voices and lived experiences and aim to create an environment where everyone feels included and supported. Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations - Do your best work here. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for this position is midnight on the 13th of September 2026. Interviews for this position are anticipated to take place on the 24th of September 2026. Please quote reference DH50644 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Candidate Pack - Global Trips Associate Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference DH50644 Category Academic-related Date published 14 August 2026 Closing date 13 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hatton-professorship-of-sustainability-la50727": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Hatton Professorship of Sustainability | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Hatton Professorship of Sustainability Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Hatton Professorship of Sustainability The Board of Electors to the Hatton Professorship of Sustainability invite applications for this Professorship from persons whose work falls within the general field of the Professorship (combining behavioural sciences and sustainability studies) to take up appointment on 1 July 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Candidates will have an outstanding research record of international stature in a relevant area of study (includes experimental psychology, social neuroscience, behavioural economics, consumer behaviour, political science, policy studies, and environmental social sciences, as well as allied disciplines). The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to the applications of research to address real world sustainability problems, working in combination with governments, businesses and civil society partners to design and monitor the impacts of interventions. They will be solution orientated with a special focus on individual, corporate and collective action towards environmental sustainability. They will be expected to demonstrate the vision, leadership, experience and enthusiasm to build on current strengths in maintaining and developing a leading research presence.  They will hold a PhD or equivalent postgraduate qualification. Standard professorial duties include teaching and research, examining, supervision and administration.  The Professor will be based in Cambridge.  A competitive salary will be offered. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Further information is available at: http://www.hr.admin.cam.ac.uk/professorships or contact the Human Resources, University Offices, The Old Schools, Cambridge, CB2 1TT, (email: professorships@admin.cam.ac.uk ). Applications, consisting of a letter of application, a statement of current and future research plans, a curriculum vitae and a publications list, along with details of three referees should be made online no later than 5 October 2026. Informal enquiries may be directed to Professor Bhaskar Vira (Convenor of Board of Electors): ProVCEducation@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference LA50727 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Office of the School of the Physical Sciences Salary Reference LA50727 Category Professorships and Directorships Date published 12 August 2026 Closing date 5 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
