    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/head-of-the-postgraduate-education-and-clinical-academic-training-section-ra50888": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Head of the Postgraduate Education and Clinical Academic Training Section | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Head of the Postgraduate Education and Clinical Academic Training Section Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Head of the Postgraduate Education and Clinical Academic Training Section Applications are invited for the post of Head of the Postgraduate Education and Clinical Academic Training Section within the Education Division of the Office of the School of Clinical Medicine. This is an exciting opportunity to lead the School's postgraduate and clinical academic programme administration. The School has approximately 1250 postgraduate students (studying mainly for a PhD, an MD, an MPhil, or an MRes) and approximately 160 clinical trainees on the Integrated Academic Training pathway (either in the National Specialised Foundation Programme, in an Academic Clinical Fellowship, or in a Clinical Lectureship). This role is central to the effective management, leadership, and administration of these programmes, and the post holder will be responsible for maintaining excellent relationships and communication with administrative, academic, and clinical staff across the School and University, and also with external partners, particularly Cambridge University Health Partners. The role holder will act as Secretary to the Postgraduate Operations Committee which reports directly to the Faculty Board of Clinical Medicine and is chaired by the School's Director of Postgraduate Education. They will also have oversight of administration for the Degree Committee for the Faculties of Clinical Medicine and Veterinary Medicine. The successful candidate will have a degree or equivalent experience, and will be an experienced administrator, preferably in a Higher Education context. They will have excellent management and team leadership skills, as well as change management skills. They will have very strong interpersonal skills and communication skills (both written and verbal), and an ability to communicate clearly and effectively with staff and students at all levels throughout the University and within the NHS, as well as with numerous other stakeholders both nationally and internationally. They will also be able to work flexibly and creatively, both independently and as part of a team, and will have the ability to rapidly assimilate new information and knowledge and meet challenging deadlines. Further information is available via the link below. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please contact Dr Litsa Biggs at FacultySec@medschl.cam.ac.uk (Head of the Education Division and line manager of the post). Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and a CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. The closing date for applications is: 20th September 2026. The interview date for the role is: 8th October 2026 Please quote reference RA50888 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Office of the School of Clinical Medicine Salary £42,254-£56,535 Reference RA50888 Category Academic-related Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 20 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
