    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-manager-temporary-cover-nr50848": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "HR Manager [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Manager [Temporary Cover] Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Manager [Temporary Cover] The Department of Computer Science and Technology is an academic department that encompasses Computer Science along with many aspects of Technology, Engineering and Mathematics.  With around 340 academic staff, researchers and PhD students, the Department has an international reputation for research excellence and innovation. Our success is built on attracting and supporting talented staff and creating a stimulating environment that promotes a strong sense of community whilst valuing and recognising individual contribution. We are seeking an experienced HR professional to join us as HR Manager on a nine-month fixed-term basis or secondment opportunity, providing cover during the secondment of the current role holder.  The successful candidate will play a key role in supporting the Department through a busy academic year. This is an excellent opportunity for an internal candidate looking to broaden their HR experience and gain exposure to a wide range of people management issues in an active teaching and research department within the School of Technology.  Applications are particularly welcomed from existing University HR professionals looking to further develop their careers. As HR Manager, you will be responsible for providing accurate and timely advice and guidance to staff on HR related matters across the employee lifecycle. In this varied and rewarding role, you will work collaboratively with senior members of the Department to develop, implement and maintain the Department's HR strategy.  You will promote best practice in line with the University's policies and procedures and support areas such as recruitment, probation, staff review and development, capability and sickness absence processes.  Key to your success in this role will be your ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues at all levels. Previous experience at HR Manager level is not essential, provided candidates can demonstrate the skills and experience required to succeed in the role.  Candidates should, however, have a strong understanding of HR policies, procedures and processes within the University of Cambridge. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Please quote reference NR50848 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. Please include your CV and a cover letter detailing your suitability for this position. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: Caroline Stewart,\nDepartmental Secretary at departmental-secretary@cst.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information HR Manager Key information Department/location Department of Computer Science and Technology Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference NR50848 Category Academic-related Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 16 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/impact-evaluation-lead-fixed-term-xn50773": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) Are you passionate about building evidence that strengthens the role of collections, culture and research to support positive change in society? The University of Cambridge Museums (UCM) is looking for an experienced and collaborative Impact Evaluation Lead to establish a new team working across the University's museums, libraries, archives and Botanic Garden. Together, the University Collections represent the UK's highest concentration of internationally important collections outside London. Through engagement, participation and research, we bring people together to explore the big questions: from the earliest forms of life to the future of our planet. Now we're investing in our ability to understand and evolve the impact of that work. Working across programmes, disciplines and communities, the Impact Evaluation Lead will develop a shared approach to evaluation to better understand the social, cultural and economic impact of participation with collections. You'll manage a specialist team to develop longitudinal approaches to evaluation, build robust datasets and insights, and support colleagues to generate, interpret and act on evidence. About You We're looking for someone with substantial experience of designing and leading evaluation teams working alongside participation and engagement with culture and collections. You'll be confident developing approaches to evaluation that generate meaningful insight over time and across diverse settings. You'll be able to use evidence to shape decision-making, strengthen practice, build capability in others and help embed learning across a complex organisation. You'll bring a strong commitment to socially just and inclusive evaluation practice, with the ability to apply approaches that support participants and communities who are underserved, underrepresented or at risk of marginalisation. If you're excited by the potential of collections, culture and research to create meaningful change, we'd love to hear from you. Benefits of working at Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service-related pay progression and annual cost of living increases Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days paid leave (including bank holidays) Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries and salary exchange schemes for childcare) An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please upload your CV and cover letter to the application. Please note that additional uploaded documents will not be considered as part of the recruitment. Informal enquiries about the role should be directed to: David Cahill Roots, Head of UCM Programmes and Collaborations, Email: dc915@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact Karin Kuchta, HR Coordinator, Email: csihhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference XN50773 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information XN50773 - Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cross School Initiative Hub Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference XN50773 Category Academic-related Date published 24 August 2026 Closing date 18 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/investigator-fixed-term-ah49916": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Investigator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Investigator (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Investigator (Fixed Term) Two positions are available: one fixed-term post funded for an initial period of 24 months, and one fixed-term maternity cover post for 13.5 months or until the return of the postholder, whichever occurs sooner. We are looking for an experienced Investigator to join the University of Cambridge's Human Resources Division, specialising in complex and sensitive staff investigations.\nThis role plays a key part in ensuring fair, thorough and proportionate investigation processes across a range of staff misconduct and complaint cases. We encourage early applications as they will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. About the role You will lead investigations into a range of staff matters, including complex and sensitive cases such as serious misconduct and complaints, ensuring findings are evidence based and clearly presented. Working closely with HR colleagues and stakeholders, you will provide expert advice, support decision making processes, and contribute to continuous improvement of investigation practices. What you will be doing Managing complex investigations from planning through to final report Interviewing parties, gathering evidence and assessing credibility Producing clear, balanced investigation reports with findings of fact Presenting findings to senior decision makers at hearings Advising stakeholders on investigation processes and risk Delivering training and contributing to improvements in practice We are looking for someone who has Strong experience conducting complex and sensitive investigations Excellent report writing and analytical skills Ability to handle sensitive issues with professionalism and discretion Strong communication and stakeholder management skills Knowledge of UK employment law, investigations and best practice High attention to detail and ability to manage competing priorities Why join us? Alongside working in a collaborative and supportive environment, the University of Cambridge offers a range of excellent benefits, including: Development opportunities such as LinkedIn Learning, job shadowing and career pathways. 41 days annual leave (including bank holidays) and a highly competitive pension scheme. Hybrid working with flexibility in how you arrange your office days. A wide range of discounts at local retailers and thousands of national brands. Health and wellbeing support, including discounted gym access and the Staff Counselling Service. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for flexible working arrangements. For this role, all applications will be managed by Spirehouse Recruitment. To apply, please send your CV to cambridge@spirehouse.co.uk For further information about the role, please contact Abbie Carr (Executive Consultant), abbie@spirehouse.co.uk Closing date: Wednesday 23 September 2026 Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Download further information Investigator - Further Information Document Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £42,254-£56,535 Reference AH49916 Category Academic-related Date published 2 September 2026 Closing date 23 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
