to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs REF Administrator (Part Time, Fixed Term) The McDonald Institute for Archaeological Research invites applications for a 0.2 FTE (7.3 hours/week)REF administrator. The role holder will work directly with the Chair and members of the Archaeology REF Committee for the University of Cambridge, and act as liaison with central university support teams. The appointee will join a thriving community of academics and professional staff, and work at the intersection between researchers and administrators to ensure a successful and timely delivery of our submission to REF. We are seeking a highly organised, self-driven individual who is familiar with REF and open access compliance, competent with ICT, and able to handle confidential information appropriately. The working pattern will be quite flexible, and agreed with the line manager. Starting date: 01/10/2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please contact Prof Marcos Martinón-Torres  ( m.martinon-torres@arch.cam.ac.uk ). Please quote reference JC50840 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location McDonald Institute for Archaeological Research Salary £33,951-£39,906 pro rata Reference JC50840 Category Assistant staff Date published 24 August 2026 