      "title": "SF Express Post-Doctoral Research Fellowship in Industrial Logistics (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "SF Express Post-Doctoral Research Fellowship in Industrial Logistics (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs SF Express Post-Doctoral Research Fellowship in Industrial Logistics (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs SF Express Post-Doctoral Research Fellowship in Industrial Logistics (Fixed Term) A position exists for a Senior Research Associate in the Department of Engineering and Darwin College, to work in the area of Industrial Logistics, holding a 5-year Research Fellowship supported by SF Express. The post holder will be located at the Institute for Manufacturing in West Cambridge. The key responsibilities and duties are to carry out research in the field of industrial logistics, work with industrial companies on supply chain logistics issues, lead programme in intelligent logistics, including teaching and supervision, and disseminate research outputs in relevant journal/conference papers. The skills, qualifications and experience required to perform the role are: A PhD in Industrial Logistics or related discipline Background in either Logistics Operations Management, Engineering Logistics Systems, Development of Logistics Technologies or software Ability to work within a team and collaborate with research sponsors and external partners, both in academia and industry; The ability to lead and coordinate research activities. As the successful candidate will also be a Research Fellow of Darwin College, they would be expected to fulfil the associated responsibilities, including (but not limited to) participating in Governing Body meetings, attending regular seminars, joining one of the College committees or potentially becoming a Graduate Tutor. Among numerous benefits Darwin Research Fellows are entitled under the College's Ordinances to dine free of charge up to seven meals each week and may claim for selected expenses related to their research. It may be possible to offer rented single-room accommodation for up to two years, subject to availability, for which a charge will be made. The successful candidate will have completed a PhD in an area relating to logistics engineering and to have demonstrated excellence in this work through publications and innovative development. Appointment at Senior Research Associate level is dependent on significant experience as a postdoctoral research associate or equivalent, with proven impact from authored publications. An understanding in the industrial or service needs in this area will be important and practical experience would be beneficial. Senior Research Associate: £43,310 - £56,535 Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 5 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV), Publication Record and a covering letter in the Upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please submit your application by midnight on the closing date. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please contact: Rebecca Evans, dial-admin@eng.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference NM50735 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further particulars Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £42,254-£56,535 Reference NM50735 Category Research Date published 12 August 2026 Closing date 16 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/teaching-associate-in-computational-linguistics-temporary-cover-gn50797": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover)",
      "description": "Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) The Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics is seeking to appoint a part-time Teaching Associate (0.5FTE) in Computational Linguistics. This role is to provide temporary cover until 30 September 2027. Educated to a PhD level, the role holder will have core technical expertise in Computational Linguistics and Natural Language Processing. Successful candidates will have prior experience of teaching delivery in this area and excellent presentation and communication skills. The role holder will be expected to contribute to the teaching, research supervision and examining for the MPhil in Linguistics and Language Sciences. They will also contribute to some teaching, supervision and examining for the Department's undergraduate course in Linguistics. They will work with the Postgraduate Administrator to monitor student attainment, wellbeing and feedback, and undertake administrative duties commensurate with the grade of the role. The successful candidate will be based at the Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics which is part of the Faculty of Modern and Medieval Languages and Linguistics. The department offers excellent theoretical and empirical research in a broad spread of fields form historical linguistics and comparative syntax to language processing and computational linguistics. It also houses the Language Technology Laboratory which conducts research in the areas of Computational Linguistics and Natural Language Processing. More information about the Department can be found at: https://www.mmll.cam.ac.uk/subjects/theoretical-and-applied-linguistics In order for your application to be considered, please upload the following documents: Covering letter Curriculum vitae, including a list of publications One article or chapter-length writing sample (max 10,000 words) Names and contact details of two referees who are familiar with your work in the relevant field. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term until 30 September 2027 or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy, you can contact Professor Anna Korhonen alk23@cam.ac.uk . If you have questions about the application process, please contact the School HR Team on MMLLPersonnel@admin.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is midnight (BST) on Tuesday 15 September 2026. Interviews will be held in the week commencing 28 September 2026, subject to change. Please quote reference GN50797 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics Salary £35,608-£46,049 pro rata Reference GN50797 Category Academic Date published 1 September 2026 Closing date 15 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
